# This module's Go sources are LF in the index and must be LF in the worktree
# too. gofmt compares the bytes ON DISK, so a CRLF checkout makes `gofmt -l`
# list a file that is byte-identical to a clean one. Measured here on
# providers.go: gofmt listed it, the file had CRLF endings, and CI on Linux
# passed green — a false positive that costs a diagnosis every time it fires.
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf=true, which is what put the CRLF there.
*.go text eol=lf

# History note: the vendored linux CLI binary used to be tracked with Git LFS
# here. The image now builds the CLI from a pinned upstream commit (see the
# Dockerfile), so the binary and vendor-cli.sh were removed together with that
# rule. The eighteen old blobs and their LFS objects stay in the history:
# removing them means rewriting history, which invalidates every existing clone
# and every commit hash. That is a separate decision.